Your family situation could 
be turned into a spectacle!

00:14:15.950 --> 00:14:17.820
What's wrong with that?

00:14:17.820 --> 00:14:20.380
I'm doing this so she'll see me.

00:14:21.380 --> 00:14:23.950
You had a normal upbringing 
in a normal family.

00:14:23.950 --> 00:14:26.130
You wouldn't understand.

00:14:27.210 --> 00:14:29.890
A normal family, huh?

00:14:52.110 --> 00:14:55.620
Judging by his behavior, 
it's clear where he's going.

00:14:55.620 --> 00:14:58.230
Yes. A lady's room.

00:14:58.230 --> 00:15:00.010
That would be what <i>you'd </i>do.

00:15:00.010 --> 00:15:03.340
There's only one place he'd go.

00:15:05.870 --> 00:15:07.350
The top floor.

00:15:09.250 --> 00:15:10.090
Wow.

00:15:10.090 --> 00:15:12.310
This is amazing.

00:15:21.580 --> 00:15:25.100
Why are we stalking him?

00:15:25.100 --> 00:15:28.310
Because we're worried about our center.

00:15:28.310 --> 00:15:31.580
Riku went to see his brother, didn't he?

00:15:31.580 --> 00:15:33.030
Won't it be an emotional reunion?

00:15:33.030 --> 00:15:38.310
Normally it would be, but Kujo's 
scarier than his cute face suggests.

00:15:38.310 --> 00:15:41.970
If it looks like Kujo-san's harsh 
words are giving him an attack,

00:15:41.970 --> 00:15:43.460
we'll give up and drag him away.

00:15:43.800 --> 00:15:44.600
Yeah.

00:15:43.810 --> 00:15:44.600
Got it.

00:15:44.600 --> 00:15:48.510
Okay. We're the rescue rangers!

00:15:49.420 --> 00:15:50.470
Oh...

00:15:56.820 --> 00:15:57.850
Tenn-nii...

00:15:57.850 --> 00:15:59.850
You're in there, aren't you?

00:16:00.510 --> 00:16:03.600
If you don't want to open the 
door, we can talk like this.

00:16:03.600 --> 00:16:04.390
Just listen.

00:16:05.030 --> 00:16:08.170
I'm trying to become an idol.

00:16:08.710 --> 00:16:11.130
We're going to be debuting soon.

00:16:11.130 --> 00:16:13.060
We're called IDOLiSH7.

00:16:13.580 --> 00:16:17.420
I wanted to get closer to you 
and learn more about you.

00:16:18.090 --> 00:16:20.270
That's why I decided to sing.

00:16:22.340 --> 00:16:26.000
There's still so much I don't know, but...

00:16:27.410 --> 00:16:29.000
Hey, Tenn-nii.

00:16:29.910 --> 00:16:33.630
Why did you abandon your family and leave?

00:16:36.180 --> 00:16:37.960
Abandoned his family and left?

00:16:37.960 --> 00:16:40.060
Someone else was inside!

00:16:40.060 --> 00:16:40.890
Huh?

00:16:40.890 --> 00:16:43.090
U-Um, I...

00:16:43.090 --> 00:16:45.180
You're IDOLiSH7's center.

00:16:45.180 --> 00:16:46.740
S-Sorry!

00:16:46.740 --> 00:16:49.940
I-I wasn't expecting anyone 
other than Tenn-nii to come out.

00:16:49.940 --> 00:16:52.310
Are you Tenn's family?

00:16:52.980 --> 00:16:54.070
Um...

00:16:54.070 --> 00:16:57.830
He never talks about himself.

00:16:57.830 --> 00:16:59.640
Well, come in.

00:16:59.640 --> 00:17:01.330
Wh-What?! Who, me?

00:17:01.330 --> 00:17:02.270
Now?

00:17:02.270 --> 00:17:03.650
Don't be shy.

00:17:03.650 --> 00:17:04.250
Wha...

00:17:05.310 --> 00:17:06.970
Wh-What should we do?

00:17:06.970 --> 00:17:08.140
Rescue him?

00:17:08.140 --> 00:17:12.830
If anything, he seemed to 
be reacting positively.

00:17:17.450 --> 00:17:18.430
What are you doing?

00:17:18.430 --> 00:17:19.890
K-Kujo Tenn!

00:17:19.890 --> 00:17:22.640
Hey, you're the kid who forgot 
to sing at <i>Music Festa</i>.

00:17:25.660 --> 00:17:26.750
Iori!

00:17:26.750 --> 00:17:29.270
Damn you! How dare you 
incapacitate my brother!

00:17:29.640 --> 00:17:31.860
What was that, you terrible dancer?

00:17:34.020 --> 00:17:35.530
Oh, Mitsuki!

00:17:36.710 --> 00:17:38.950
No... he's not responding!

00:17:38.950 --> 00:17:40.410
Time for an emergency operation!

00:17:40.410 --> 00:17:41.330
Scalpel!

00:17:42.010 --> 00:17:43.580
You're playing doctor?

00:17:43.910 --> 00:17:46.560
So, what are you doing here?

00:17:46.560 --> 00:17:47.330
Spying on us?

00:17:47.330 --> 00:17:50.900
N-No, we just happened to be in the area.

00:17:50.900 --> 00:17:52.500
We were just on our way back.

00:17:52.500 --> 00:17:53.730
Oh, really?

00:17:53.730 --> 00:17:57.260
I'm not sure how you just happen 
to be on the top floor, though.

00:17:57.610 --> 00:18:00.020
Is it okay if we abandon Riku?

00:18:00.020 --> 00:18:01.900
I know it's hard, but we have to.

00:18:01.900 --> 00:18:04.100
We can't sacrifice anyone else.

00:18:05.710 --> 00:18:08.180
Later, Kujo. Goodnight.

00:18:15.470 --> 00:18:17.850
There's something I want to tell you.

00:18:17.850 --> 00:18:22.340
About that sloppy <i>Music Festa</i> and 
your attitude as professionals.

00:18:22.810 --> 00:18:23.870
Actually, we—

00:18:24.230 --> 00:18:26.110
I'll order room service for you.

00:18:27.300 --> 00:18:29.580
But in exchange, you'll 
 sit upright on the floor.

00:18:31.700 --> 00:18:33.170
Dead end.

00:18:37.010 --> 00:18:38.300
We're back!

00:18:38.300 --> 00:18:40.780
We brought you souvenirs from Okinawa!

00:18:41.390 --> 00:18:43.380
Did something happen?

00:18:43.380 --> 00:18:44.850
Actually...

00:18:45.620 --> 00:18:47.020
What is this?

00:18:53.580 --> 00:18:55.810
The place has been ransacked.

00:18:55.810 --> 00:18:57.430
Seems like a thief.

00:18:57.430 --> 00:18:58.950
President! Ogami-san!

00:18:58.950 --> 00:19:01.840
Welcome back. Surprised?

00:19:01.840 --> 00:19:03.120
What is this?

00:19:03.120 --> 00:19:09.040
I know you just got back, but could you 
check to see if anything's missing?

00:19:09.040 --> 00:19:11.700
The police gave us 
permission to go inside.

00:19:11.700 --> 00:19:12.610
Okay!

00:19:12.610 --> 00:19:14.670
We'll help clean.

00:19:15.050 --> 00:19:17.090
Thanks. We appreciate it.

00:19:17.090 --> 00:19:18.890
Was anything stolen?

00:19:20.330 --> 00:19:23.340
All the important documents 
and valuables seem to be fine.

00:19:23.340 --> 00:19:24.180
It's not here!

00:19:24.490 --> 00:19:26.930
I can't find the demo tape
 for our debut song!

00:19:28.620 --> 00:19:29.830
The debut song?

00:19:30.260 --> 00:19:33.560
We still have the data, so it should be fine.

00:19:33.560 --> 00:19:37.620
No thief would steal just a song, right?

00:19:37.620 --> 00:19:39.370
No, we can't be sure.

00:19:39.370 --> 00:19:43.340
Their songs are just that valuable.

00:19:44.390 --> 00:19:47.350
I hope nothing bad comes from this.

00:19:50.940 --> 00:19:55.430
You really went with a new 
direction on our new song.

00:19:55.430 --> 00:19:56.570
That's fine.

00:19:56.570 --> 00:19:58.340
I'm sure it'll be fun at concerts.

00:20:00.980 --> 00:20:02.590
What's wrong, Tenn?

00:20:03.930 --> 00:20:06.800
Hyuga-san, you wrote this song, right?

00:20:07.730 --> 00:20:09.600
O-Of course.

00:20:09.600 --> 00:20:13.090
One day later, and I would've 
hired someone else.

00:20:16.410 --> 00:20:19.900
You'll be even busier preparing for 
the announcement of your new song.

00:20:19.900 --> 00:20:25.320
We'll erase all mention of IDOLiSH7's 
debut with TRIGGER's new song.

00:20:26.990 --> 00:20:28.830
Thank you, everybody!

00:20:29.150 --> 00:20:31.170
Our next song will be our last one.

00:20:31.170 --> 00:20:33.580
Besides, the trains are running today.

00:20:35.080 --> 00:20:36.580
<b>I love I7</b>

00:20:36.950 --> 00:20:38.300
Riku-kun!

00:20:38.300 --> 00:20:40.090
You're all so cool!

00:20:40.090 --> 00:20:45.900
For everyone here gathered today, we'll 
perform our new song before it goes on sale.

00:20:45.900 --> 00:20:46.860
A new song?

00:20:46.860 --> 00:20:48.370
They're singing a new song!

00:20:48.370 --> 00:20:52.060
I have a feeling this song 
will be special for us.

00:20:52.470 --> 00:20:57.360
We've decided to sing it for our supporters 
because we really want you to hear it.

00:20:58.570 --> 00:21:00.020
Thank you!

00:21:00.020 --> 00:21:02.280
Thank you!

00:21:02.610 --> 00:21:04.780
No, thank you!

00:21:03.770 --> 00:21:04.780
Thank you.

